    feat(board): plural association fields (pull_requests/branches/worktrees) with validation and merge semantics (BT-077)
    
    Additive structured plural fields so a task can track multiple associated PRs,
    branches and worktrees across the dimensions involved, without losing existing
    singular worktree/branch fields or sessions.
    
    - internal/board/associations.go: association types, PR URL/number identity
      normalization (accept GitHub PR URL or bare number; reject malformed values),
      merge-without-overwrite semantics per dimension
    - internal/board/keys.go, validate.go, write.go: schema + validation + write
      path support; legacy singular-only rows still parse/validate
    - cmd/boardctl/main.go: create/update/show/list/search/render/export expose
      the plural fields; adding one PR keeps existing PRs and other dimensions
    - tests: multi-value per dimension, legacy rows, sibling preservation,
      normalization rules, malformed rejection, CLI-level round-trip
    
    Verified: go build/vet/test ./... green, gofmt clean; throwaway-board probe
    (2 PRs + 2 branches + 2 worktrees accumulate; 3rd PR merge preserves siblings;
    export/import round-trip; validate+doctor OK); legacy-row probe passes.
    
